   (:evidence (vector "DAW passes 13 tests and 50 assertions; NLE passes 14 tests and 51 assertions, including deterministic relative-path selection, exact hash matching and legacy filename fallback."
              "Both shadow-cljs production releases completed through the repository resource guard."
              "Chrome directory E2E loaded projects with registered SHA-256 media, presented same-name wrong-content files beside nested renamed exact-content files, and reported 1 matched, 0 missing and 1 ignored in each application."
              "DAW decoded the selected WAV and started real Web Audio playback; NLE rebuilt a Blob URL, reached decoder-ready state and wrote the recovered MP4 to its verified IndexedDB cache."
              "Browser and local HTTP server lifecycles were closed after verification."
              "Both application pull requests were reviewed and squash-merged."
              "The required freshness and ledger verifier scripts are absent from this root revision; direct EDN parsing verified accepted status and the supersedes target."))))
  (:adr/consequences
  (vector "Users can recover moved or renamed project media by selecting a parent directory instead of picking every file individually."
   "A same-name file cannot replace a hash-bearing project asset unless its complete SHA-256 digest matches."
   "Candidate ordering is reproducible across selection order, while unreferenced files never become project assets implicitly."
   "Browser directory access remains user-initiated per selection; persistent directory handles are a separate follow-up capability."))
